<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Internal Macedonian Revolutionary Organization</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1893–1934</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as IMRO, Internal Macedonian-Adrianople Revolutionary Organisation</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Internal Macedonian Revolutionary Organization was a secret revolutionary society founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaloniki">Thessaloniki</a> in 1893 to win autonomy for Macedonia and the Adrianople region from Ottoman rule. In 1903 it launched the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilinden-preobrazhenie-uprising">Ilinden Uprising</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonia-region">Macedonia</a>, during which rebels proclaimed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krusevo">Kruševo</a> Republic, and the Preobrazhenie Uprising in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a>, which created the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strandzha">Strandzha</a> Commune. Both were crushed by Ottoman troops. The organisation later split into factions and was suppressed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> in 1934.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/internal-macedonian-revolutionary-organization.jpg" alt="Internal Macedonian Revolutionary Organization" width="320" height="337" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Maxim Bluecher · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IMRO_badge.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
